  "verdict": "scale_word is NOT buildable under the unit_swap discipline from either approved source. Prose co-locates the scale word with its numeral, so the large families are adjacency-solvable (the H148 rule forbids exactly this). The two adjacency-proof constructions are supply-blocked: the caption route is single-direction (EDGAR writes 'in thousands' at volume and 'in millions' rarely, and the minority direction needs the majority word present as a distractor), and the identical-numeral route yields tens of items, not thousands. InfoTabs carries no scale captions at all."
